{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1124848-hermetics-without-ritual-or-tools","id":1124848,"title":"Hermetics without ritual or tools","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-04T11:32:59-07:00","id":1124848,"title":"Hermetics without ritual or tools","content":"There are several things I am fond of and admire about the way the OoH does things, including their vision of metaphysics that puts humanity and human Will front and center, their inclusive, practical, and meritocratic attitude towards membership and mysticism (elitism is OK as long as it is earned), and their uncompromising drive for self-empowerment and self-improvement. On the other hand, I absolutely cannot contemplate playing a mage whose foci system is significantly based on cumbersome physical trappings and tools, or slow and complex rituals. I'm not any fond of mechanistic paradigms (or theistic ones, for that matter), either. So in the light of M20 foci rules and guidelines I've been pondering how to develop characters that may have recognizable Hermetic features and are compliant with my preferences. They may or may not be official (if unorthodox) OoH members; they might also be Orphans or members of other groups I fancy (e.g. Akashayana, Chakravanti, Verbena, Sahajiya) with hybrid foci systems that include Hermetic elements.<br /> <br /> Possible paradigms (either used separately or more likely in combination) might be: Everything is an Illusion (Gnosticism seems to have a place in Hermetic thinking); Might is Right (very appropriate for the OoH); Transcend Your Limits (antinomian praxis); We\u2019re All God(s) in Disguise (extension and combination of the above); maybe even Creation is Divine and Alive (I'm not sure how much immanent pantheism fits Hermetic ideology) and Consciousness is the Only True Reality (a variant of Gnosticism).<br /> <br /> Possible practices (likely at least 3-4 of them, quite possibly an half-dozen) might include: Art of Desire, bardism, chaos magick, dominion, invigoration, martial arts, maleficia, psionics, and yoga (only the portions of those practices that are not seriously based on rituals or tools). High Ritual might or might not have a place at all depending how much it can be made well, not ritual. Alchemy seems too materialistic to fit. Craftwork, hypertech, and weird science are simply unacceptable.<br /> <br /> Possible instruments (likely ranging from seven to a baker's dozen or so) may include: bodywork; dance, gestures, and movement; elements; energy; eye contact; language, music, and voice; math and numerology; meditation; ordeals and extertions; sex and sensuality; symbols; social dominations; thought forms; True Names; wands and staves; weapons; writing and inscriptions. I tend to merge variants of instruments that share the same basic feature (e.g. movement, voice, or numbers) within the same instrument, as long as all of them seem to fit within the character's foci system. My preferred instruments typically involve actions that may be performed on the fly rather than physical objects or rituals. However a few tools might be acceptable if they are especially easy to find, use, or replace, or they provide special benefits too good to give up (e.g. weapons for combat magick).<br /> <br /> Do you have any constructive comments or suggestions?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T18:36:21-07:00","id":1125040,"title":"","content":"Chuck the M20 foci rules and guidelines under a bus?<br /> <br /> This might not seem particularly constructive, but it really is the best way to deal with them.<br /> <br /> As for how to run a Hermetic, just grab a single magic wand. Or maybe a crystal or something else suitably mystic to wave around Or maybe just use hand gestures. Combine with short and sweet incantations invoking whatever cosmic force you wish to alter.<br /> <br /> &quot;Orsanai!&quot; *waves a hand at the car with thumb and index finger extended away from the remainder.* now that car is on fire. For more ritualistic prepared stuff, just carry around chalk to sketch barriers or sigils or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T22:24:43-07:00","id":1125103,"title":"","content":"Read Dresden Files, take notes, profit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T08:55:22-07:00","id":1125247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1124848-hermetics-without-ritual-or-tools?p=1125103#post1125103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Read Dresden Files, take notes, profit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't. The so-called Laws of Magic piss me off into ragequitting. I absolutely cannot stand a setting where fundamentalist Judeo-Christian morality, anti-magic prejudice, and fantastic racism are written into cosmic law, characters are threatened all the time with summary execution or descent into madness if they indulge in normal PC activities such as using lethal magic, body transformation, mind-reading, mental control, or necromancy w/o any concern for circumstances like self-defence, necessity, or consent, and mortals are the chosen race that is possessed of free will and deserving of protection from abuse, while it is OK to mistreat the other supernatural sapients because they are slaves to their nature. Dresden Files can rot on the shelf for all that I care. By the way, I read and really appreciated other fantasy works of the same author where the LoM are not an issue, such as Codex Alera; for me it is really unfortunate and a pity that the author chose to add such a screwed-up setting element I cannot really stand to DF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 08-05-2017, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T10:38:14-07:00","id":1125274,"title":"","content":"Hermetics were in the Songs of Science volume of the Traditions Gathered, one of the Mage 1e(2e perhaps) compilations of Tradition books. Hermetics do a little of ritual and use foci because it makes magic easier. While not modern scientists, Hermetics plan on being around for a long time and are systematic. Thus they've developed a lot of procedures to do magick--part of which may come from Ars Magicka.<br /> <br /> You can certainly toss the tools from M20, as those are a newer way to handle things than in previous Mage incarnations, but when we think of wizards and their wonders, they usually have tools. A sufficiently skilled Hermetic can dispense with tools, but since there are mythic threads like the wizard doing magic with crystal or the magic wand, it helps Hermetics succeed on their magickal works more often.<br /> <br /> Alchemy works for the medieval alchemist types, like House Solificati. Alchemy also holds a spiritual component, as it's not just about changing lead to gold but also about perfecting oneself. Craftwork seems like a House Verditius thing--those Hermetics make amazing traps and material goods to do their magick. Hypertech might work for those in House Thig or House Xaos, but those are definitely outliers as they were but 20ish-member houses in recent times. Weird science does seem to be more a Sons of Ether think.<br /> <br /> Enochian and other high ritual magick isn't going to be used for a simple, on the spot effect. Getting a sanctum ready, summoning spirits, or casting a major spell require a lot of successes. Ritual is good for this, especially if there are some apprentices or true believers helping out.<br /> <br /> If one does not like the Hermetics as written, they can be changed. An easy way to handle this would be to have an ex Miscellena house for an OOH member who's not big into all the rituals, because Ex Miscellena has the most diverse magickal practices as it is the 'hodgepodge.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T14:31:16-07:00","id":1125352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1124848-hermetics-without-ritual-or-tools?p=1125247#post1125247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't. The so-called Laws of Magic piss me off into ragequitting. I absolutely cannot stand a setting where fundamentalist Judeo-Christian morality, anti-magic prejudice, and fantastic racism are written into cosmic law, characters are threatened all the time with summary execution or descent into madness if they indulge in normal PC activities such as using lethal magic, body transformation, mind-reading, mental control, or necromancy w/o any concern for circumstances like self-defence, necessity, or consent, and mortals are the chosen race that is possessed of free will and deserving of protection from abuse, while it is OK to mistreat the other supernatural sapients because they are slaves to their nature. Dresden Files can rot on the shelf for all that I care. By the way, I read and really appreciated other fantasy works of the same author where the LoM are not an issue, such as Codex Alera; for me it is really unfortunate and a pity that the author chose to add such a screwed-up setting element I cannot really stand to DF.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I'm not Christian and not even religious, but the LoM didn't bother me nearly as much. They're bit harsh and the Council is quite a bigoted bunch (which Harry remarked frequently and had plenty of conflicts with them), but otherwise yeah, I'm okay with certain kinds of magic being off-limit (and as far as I remember, lethal magic isn't among them, nor body transformation, however black magic is and necromancy is traditionally black magic, we just got accustomed to it via D&amp;D). That human wizards are prejudiced toward humans? Spoiler alert: MtAs mages too.<br /> <br /> But at the end, it doesn't mater, really. If you found the books that abrasive to your sensibilities you rage-quited (really? I never rage-quited a book), that's totally your choice, I just thought your points were a bit excessive here and there. I don't want to convince you to like the books, or anything. <br /> <br /> There's another series: <a href=\"http://benedictjacka.co.uk/alex-verus/\" target=\"_blank\">http://benedictjacka.co.uk/alex-verus/</a> I didn't get the time to start yet, but I heard good things about it. I don't know how close to Hermetics the character is, but I imagine, if it's using traditional western wizardry trappings, it would has some of the gist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T17:37:58-07:00","id":1125736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1124848-hermetics-without-ritual-or-tools?p=1125040#post1125040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chuck the M20 foci rules and guidelines under a bus?<br /> <br /> This might not seem particularly constructive, but it really is the best way to deal with them.<br /> <br /> As for how to run a Hermetic, just grab a single magic wand. Or maybe a crystal or something else suitably mystic to wave around Or maybe just use hand gestures. Combine with short and sweet incantations invoking whatever cosmic force you wish to alter.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Orsanai!&amp;quot; *waves a hand at the car with thumb and index finger extended away from the remainder.* now that car is on fire. For more ritualistic prepared stuff, just carry around chalk to sketch barriers or sigils or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;On the other hand, I absolutely cannot contemplate playing a mage whose foci system is significantly based on cumbersome physical trappings and tools, or slow and complex rituals. I'm not any fond of mechanistic paradigms (or theistic ones, for that matter), either.&quot;<br /> <br /> The OP specifically mentions how they don't want to use physical tools or slow complex rituals, and you proceed to suggest physical tools they can use. Your comment isn't constructive to the conversation on any level.<br /> <br /> To the OP, I think that you'll do well to make a character from one of the other organizations and implement the facets of the Order of Hermes that you do like. Bonus points if you write into your background that you were chosen to join the Order, but decided you were better off with one of the other Traditions instead. There is plenty of potential for a love/hate relationship with the Hermetics for such a character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T20:00:24-07:00","id":1125768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PazuzuAxelf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1124848-hermetics-without-ritual-or-tools?p=1125736#post1125736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;On the other hand, I absolutely cannot contemplate playing a mage whose foci system is significantly based on cumbersome physical trappings and tools, or slow and complex rituals. I'm not any fond of mechanistic paradigms (or theistic ones, for that matter), either.&quot;<br /> <br /> The OP specifically mentions how they don't want to use physical tools or slow complex rituals, and you proceed to suggest physical tools they can use. Your comment isn't constructive to the conversation on any level.<br /> <br /> To the OP, I think that you'll do well to make a character from one of the other organizations and implement the facets of the Order of Hermes that you do like. Bonus points if you write into your background that you were chosen to join the Order, but decided you were better off with one of the other Traditions instead. There is plenty of potential for a love/hate relationship with the Hermetics for such a character.</div> </div> </div> </div>A wand the size of an over large pencil is not a &quot;Cumbersome physical trapping or tool&quot; It's a small easily used physical trapping and tool. Magic Words are not a 'slow complex ritual' You could bark out an incantation pretty quickly if you needed to. Perhaps not QUITE as fast as you could pull a trigger, but still.<br /> <br /> Trying to claim something as small and inobtrusive as a wand or a necklace is a &quot;Cumbersome Physical Trapping or Tool&quot; is inane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T05:09:16-07:00","id":1125849,"title":"","content":"As a rule, I prefer to minimize the use of physical objects as tools as much as possible, and even more so slow, complex rituals. Small, portable, easy to use or hide physical tools are reluctantly allowed, but they'd better be secondary in the character's foci system. So something like a wand, dice, cards, or jewelry might be acceptable like 10% of the time, but absolutely not if they were to be used all the time as in Harry Potter's world. The desired standard for my mage characters is they may be thrown naked in an empty cell, and they retain 90% of their magickal power if they are not also bound, gagged, and drugged into inability to think straight. Weapons may also get a pass because of the special benefits they provide for combat magic, unless the character also uses martial arts of course, but they'd better be something like a dagger rather than a broadsword.<br /> <br /> Actions that can be performed reasonably quickly on the fly and in the field without any special preparations like gestures, incantations, singing, dancing, centering for meditation, doing calculations in one's head, eye contact, invocation of True Names, focusing on a thought form, or tracing runes in the air are of course acceptable. Anything that requires a laboratory like alchemy or craftwork is simply unaccepable for anything short of creating a Wonder or making a long-term pact with a spirit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 08-07-2017, 08:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T05:48:31-07:00","id":1125867,"title":"","content":"Thinking about what i have read about modern Western magick, I think that it makes sense for a beginning hermetic to use their tools, but a more advanced one may discard them. It is considered more difficult for hermetics to cast spells without words, gestures, and rituals. For many modern practitioners these are understood to be foci for the will (as in mage). Therefore, it is very possible to work without them. Although it would be more difficult <br /> I think that the &quot;working without a focus&quot; and &quot;growing beyond the tools&quot; sections model this quite well.<br /> <br /> While instruments are important, many modern hermetics also tend to be quite eclectic, so it is possible to use almost any instrument as a focus. It's all about the symbolism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7061-azrael","name":"Azrael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7061_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T06:25:02-07:00","id":1125877,"title":"","content":"OP, I share every opinion you just posted so mich that it's scary. It's like im posting, if i couldn't see your nick and date of pot i would think it was one of my old topics.<br /> <br /> As i share your preferences, including the OoH tradition and their view on magick (but not their ritualistic practices) i recommend you to use psionics, cjaos magick and martial arts as practices. Instruments could be gestures, energy,meditation, eye contact,ordeals and exertions,voice and vocalisation,weapons. <br /> I see that you have already chosen the best practices and instruments, so I'm not quite sure what you want...<br /> <br /> Regarding high ritual and hermetics, i believe you can pick a house that isn't much focused at this practice. Or try to merge high ritual with the kind of focus you want (would like to know opinions on this too). Or, you could just not take high ritual. I think it's not mandatory, even though the majority of hermetics use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T08:28:52-07:00","id":1125916,"title":"","content":"As suggested by lord Revan, psionics make a lot of sense. Some of the rituals in hermetic magick are said to be able to awaken psychic abilities. So this is easily justified. <br /> <br /> Visualization would be workable as it is an important skill for pathworking techniques used by a Western magicians, and also for the Art of Memory.<br /> <br /> Energy work is a possibility for kabbalah-based workings. The sephiroth can be seen as a Chakra-like system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7061-azrael","name":"Azrael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7061_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}